content:
Looking at the two identical L‑shaped pieces, each covers a fixed number of unit squares. Checking each option, the outlines in A, B, C and E can all be assembled by placing the two pieces in suitable rotations (stacking, side‑by‑side, or interlocking their arms).

The shape in D, however, has a long column with two tabs protruding on the same side in positions that force one piece to be mirrored (flipped over) in order to fit — and the tabs' placement leaves an odd leftover region that no rotation of the piece can cover. Since flipping is not allowed, D cannot be formed.

\boxed{D}
